{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788419577105,"sessionID":"ses_f99e39b61ffeVhyL6wKpvNfEvS","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"task","callID":"call_3c833a974b414265b1b5c987","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Explore configuration loading system","prompt":"I need to understand the configuration file loading system. Please:\n\n1. Find the main configuration file loading implementation (look for files related to \"load\", \"config\", \"env\", or \"environment\")\n2. Identify how the `load_file` method works\n3. Find how environment-based filtering/layering currently works\n4. Look for any existing documentation (README, docs folder, docstrings)\n5. Find the current version information\n\nReturn a summary of:\n- Main file(s) containing the configuration loading logic\n- How environment processing currently works\n- Where documentation is located\n- Current version number","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"<task id=\"ses_f99e3918bffezVLS40ph59ZIkc\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\n\n\nBased on my analysis of the Dynaconf codebase, here's a comprehensive summary of the configuration file loading system:\n\n## Summary\n\n### Main Files Containing Configuration Loading Logic\n\n1. **`dynaconf/base.py`** - Core Settings class with primary loading logic:\n   - `load_file()` - Programmatically loads files from specified paths\n   - `execute_loaders()` - Orchestrates all loaders\n   - `setenv()` - Changes environment and reloads\n   - `load_includes()` - Processes included files\n\n2. **`dynaconf/loaders/`** - Multiple loader implementations:\n   - `__init__.py` - Contains `settings_loader()`, `default_loader()`, and external loader enablement\n   - `env_loader.py` - Environment variable loading with prefix filtering\n   - `base.py` - `BaseLoader` class with `_load_all_envs()` and `_envless_load()` methods\n   - Format-specific loaders: `toml_loader.py`, `yaml_loader.py`, `json_loader.py`, `ini_loader.py`, `py_loader.py`\n\n3. **`dynaconf/default_settings.py`** - Default configuration values loaded from environment variables\n\n### How `load_file` Method Works\n\nThe `load_file()` method (base.py, line 1300-1410):\n1. Takes a path (single file, list, or glob pattern)\n2. Resolves paths relative to `ROOT_PATH_FOR_DYNACONF`, last loaded file directory, or CWD\n3. Separates `.local.` files from regular files\n4. Creates `SourceMetadata` for tracking load source\n5. Delegates to `settings_loader()` which cascades through format-specific loaders\n\n### Environment Processing (Layering)\n\nEnvironment-based filtering works through:\n\n1. **`build_env_list()`** (utils/__init__.py, line 384-408):\n   - Builds a list of environments to load in order: default, global, then current env(s)\n   - Supports comma-separated envs (e.g., `production,staging`)\n\n2. **`_load_all_envs()`** (base.py loader, line 130-176):\n   - Splits file data by environment sections (e.g., `[development]`, `[production]`)\n   - Loads each matching environment's settings\n   - Uses `SourceMetadata` to track which env data came from\n\n3. **Key Settings**:\n   - `ENVIRONMENTS_FOR_DYNACONF` - Enable/disable layered environments (default: False)\n   - `ENV_FOR_DYNACONF` - Current active env (default: \"DEVELOPMENT\")\n   - `DEFAULT_ENV_FOR_DYNACONF` - Default/fallback env (default: \"DEFAULT\")\n\n4. **Environment Variable Loading**:\n   - `env_loader.py` loads variables with `ENVVAR_PREFIX_FOR_DYNACONF` prefix\n   - Supports `IGNORE_UNKNOWN_ENVVARS_FOR_DYNACONF` to limit to known vars\n   - `FILTER_STRATEGY` can transform loaded env data\n\n### Documentation Locations\n\n- **`/testbed/README.md`** - Main README with usage examples\n- **`/testbed/docs/`** - Full documentation:\n  - `configuration.md` - All configuration options\n  - `settings_files.md` - File loading details\n  - `envvars.md` - Environment variable handling\n  - `merging.md` - Merge strategies\n  - `cli.md` - Command line interface\n  - `api.md` - API reference\n- **Docstrings** - Inline documentation in base.py and loaders\n\n### Current Version\n\n**3.3.0-dev0** (as of `/testbed/dynaconf/VERSION`)\n\n---\n\nThe system is designed around the Unix philosophy of allowing environment variables to override file-based configuration, with support for multiple environments, flexible file formats, and extensible loaders.\n</task_result>\n</task>","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_f99e39b61ffeVhyL6wKpvNfEvS","sessionId":"ses_f99e3918bffezVLS40ph59ZIkc","model":{"modelID":"inception/mercury-2.5-preview","providerID":"openrouter"},"truncated":false},"title":"Explore configuration loading system","time":{"start":1788419534458,"end":1788419577095}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_0661c6d93001r5pcy3lf2RoIHB","sessionID":"ses_f99e39b61ffeVhyL6wKpvNfEvS","messageID":"msg_0661c67b5001ctYvZMNP7pM302"}}
