{"type":"text","timestamp":1788419660822,"sessionID":"ses_f99e39b61ffeVhyL6wKpvNfEvS","part":{"id":"prt_0661e5b0f001353S4r293qG0v2","messageID":"msg_0661e55e3001AhVzCzCw60oRye","sessionID":"ses_f99e39b61ffeVhyL6wKpvNfEvS","type":"text","text":"\n\nThe implementation is complete. Here's a summary of what was added:\n\n## Changes Made\n\n### 1. Core functionality (`/testbed/dynaconf/base.py`)\n- Modified `load_file()` to accept `env=False` parameter\n- When `env=False` is passed, it's internally mapped to `\"_envless\"` marker\n\n### 2. Loader handling (`/testbed/dynaconf/loaders/base.py`)\n- `BaseLoader.__init__()` now detects the `\"_envless\"` marker and sets `_envless` flag\n- `BaseLoader.load()` uses `_envless_load()` when this flag is True, bypassing environment filtering\n\n### 3. Documentation (`/testbed/docs/settings_files.md`)\n- Added section explaining `load_file(env=False)` usage\n- Clear examples showing the difference between env-aware and env-agnostic loading\n\n## Usage Example\n\n```python\nsettings = Dynaconf(environments=True)\n\n# Only loads production section (current environment)\nsettings.load_file(\"config.toml\")\n\n# Loads ALL sections from the file\nsettings.load_file(\"config.toml\", env=False)\n```\n\nThis feature:\n- Available from version 3.2.11\n- Works regardless of `ENVIRONMENTS_FOR_DYNACONF` setting\n- Loads all sections as nested dictionaries (e.g., `settings.DEVELOPMENT.db_host`)\n- Maintains all other behaviors like validation and source tracking","time":{"start":1788419660559,"end":1788419660819}}}
